#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 720.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116120} :activity/id #uuid "3b658871-23f8-5b8d-92ee-5294fec9bba3" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048445 :topic/id #uuid "a01c36d3-5643-5685-845e-29c37e89238f" :topic/math-academy-id 1733} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116120 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116493 :tutorial/content "We can use Gaussian elimination to find the general solutions of systems with any number of equations and variables. For instance, consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y+z=1, \\\\ y+3z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis system has the augmented matrix\n![](images/8a/8a8452587098eed9b697c3999c356359b949429f29ce16af2c81cf728be9480e.svg)\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\, & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+4z=1 \\\\ y+3z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable $z.$ From the second equation, we get $y=-3z,$ and from the first equation, we obtain $x=1-4z.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1-4z, \\\\ y=-3z, \\\\ z=z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1-4z \\\\ -3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+z[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "3eff050b-e4ba-52e5-aa10-7bba2feef2fc" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3162 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "6022e9b9-60ab-5ac5-b16a-17583fa649c3" :step/math-academy-id 17213 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116121}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116121 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115241 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115070 :question/id #uuid "dc6dd9b4-de7f-52d0-8ff9-a7a7f7a9abd7" :question/math-academy-id "e-4711"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d81e3f1-d930-59ee-b439-2a3645aebb6c" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048742}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115751} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115830} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266111} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266112} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302108} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302193} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326924} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400625} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402009} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402756} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186417081}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Consistent System of Equations Using Gauss-Jordan Elimination"} :step/id #uuid "79bb6bd1-8c36-5f56-9575-8a1b8388eb57" :step/math-academy-id 17214 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116122}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116122 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116494 :tutorial/content "Recall that a system of linear equations is called **consistent** if it has at least one solution. Otherwise, if there are no solutions, the system is called **inconsistent**. \n\nFor a consistent system, \n\n- the system is called **consistent independent** if the solution is unique, while\n\n- the system is called **consistent dependent** if there are infinitely many solutions.\n\n![](images/f5/f5b808eac6e1d865b13b68ce2a4f7d317560ae3965928e478531fcd2148c2c6b.png)" :tutorial/id #uuid "e0c85152-daea-5a87-a3ba-81870558c7a2" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3163 :tutorial/title "Consistent and Inconsistent Systems of Linear Equations"} :step/id #uuid "2fa6eba1-6298-51b5-bbc9-bd8c46a79468" :step/math-academy-id 17215 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116209}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116123 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115242 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115071 :question/id #uuid "f2c7cfd3-da43-5208-bd0e-21692357fabe" :question/math-academy-id "e-4712"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "22733f71-de4a-5058-a41c-039e66e333c5" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115753} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115831} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266116} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266117} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266118} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266119} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266120} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302109} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302143} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344961} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344969} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344971} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398982} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186417082} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425949} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492874}] :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Value of a Constant for Which a Given Linear System Is Consistent or Inconsistent"} :step/id #uuid "1d1a97f8-c872-5285-b963-d1938948df37" :step/math-academy-id 17216} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116209 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115299 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115124 :question/id #uuid "cd56314d-f45a-55be-9762-983fe507a1a0" :question/math-academy-id "e-6173"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9469d5c-e097-590c-8ddb-2c7fda353fac" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050240}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115752} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115832} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266113} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266114} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266115} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344956} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344957} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363108} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364365} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400632} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400639} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400646} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402763} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186403787} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492840}] :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a System as Consistent Dependent, Consistent Independent, or Inconsistent"} :step/id #uuid "e80cfcd9-1219-52d8-96c7-0ee06cdf52fc" :step/math-academy-id 23072 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116123}}] :activity/title "Gaussian Elimination For NxM Systems of Equations" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186115479}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046659} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425950} :activity/id #uuid "080f971c-621c-5ccf-b883-b98c49745b79" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048445 :topic/id #uuid "a01c36d3-5643-5685-845e-29c37e89238f" :topic/math-academy-id 1733} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425950 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425949 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17602323-8777-51fe-9a70-fac173438e8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425938} {:answer/id #uuid "3745dd5b-bc8f-5c5f-bfbb-0a70d0ee8eee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425940} {:answer/id #uuid "8c1862b9-030a-5755-b668-e59ca4c9e456" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425944} {:answer/id #uuid "a1294db0-0da9-5a02-b9e5-791ef34dcf11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425946} {:answer/id #uuid "cf6dc1f0-4ead-53bf-8e9f-9b57805aa51d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425947}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425947} :answer-field/id #uuid "80130b9b-78a0-54cc-bf84-e036ce6c2ff0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425948}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "db005b4e-86cd-5194-b2fd-10ca4ee59c03" :question/math-academy-id "q-42021" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is consistent dependent:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y=3 \\\\ -3x-(k+1)y=-9\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -3 & -(k+1) & -9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -(k+1) & -9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -k+5 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}1-2y=3 \\\\ -(k-5)y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is consistent dependent if it has infinitely many solutions. For the system to have infinitely many solutions, it must have at least one free variable.\n\nIf $k=5,$ then the second equation is $0=0,$ which is true for any value of $y$, and we can remove this equation from the system. As a result, the system will contain only one equation, $x+2y=3.$ \n\nThen, the basic variable will be $x,$ and we will have a free variable $y.$ That means the system will have infinitely many solutions.\n\nTherefore, our system is consistent dependent when $k=5.$"} :step/id #uuid "2c3254d8-7342-5cba-aa85-c696386c710a" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425952}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425951 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115832 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e1eee681-520d-5d0a-802e-8d5b29c52974" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438296} {:answer/id #uuid "b2ace7b5-89a9-5ece-ad6b-0ce43e80a049" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438297}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186438297} :answer-field/id #uuid "07e35039-20ea-5f8c-9889-aaf209c08f8c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439177} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c3d1f45-fc1a-5e10-a017-8a9199b3e295" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438298} {:answer/id #uuid "039beb6d-4028-5582-9983-702125a74145" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438299}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186438298} :answer-field/id #uuid "168dcfad-47ff-5ee1-9214-61e870c730b0" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439178} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae82757c-5e4b-593d-84dd-aca1302ca366" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438300} {:answer/id #uuid "8f20a360-4b99-5b18-808c-9bab5fd09713" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438301}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186438300} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b7ded78-a4d6-5805-8398-330746f91418" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439179}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e80c83a9-9107-528b-af57-73287d15e8e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-42061" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned} & x-3y+z=0 \\\\  & -4x+6y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent dependent\n\n- **II.** The system has no solution\n\n- **III.** The system is consistent independent" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 6 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 6 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we can to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*. \n\nAs a result, only statement I is true."} :step/id #uuid "3b9e4957-843e-5d56-8704-c60e6e8f032c"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425952 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115831 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "359439f2-81e1-5ced-8482-b2cf08a71409" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425939} {:answer/id #uuid "478b28da-a8a3-51e4-963d-8ac53adc010e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425941} {:answer/id #uuid "545c0eb7-c35a-5d44-b8e2-b045ff203715" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425942} {:answer/id #uuid "684ddf9d-dd44-5397-b1a8-e6e3ca6a2f95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425943} {:answer/id #uuid "9720657d-4e06-51f7-8e91-da074201b940" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425945}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425941} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3a07998-8f4c-5e30-bdee-b2acbf389fbd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113923}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "84cf8820-fa64-5d50-9d9c-d3a9404788a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-42059" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned} & 2x+3y=1 \\\\  & 6x+(k+3)y=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 6 & k+3 & -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 6 & k+3 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & k-6 & -8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+3y=1 \\\\ (k-6)y=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=6,$ then the second equation is $0=-8,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=6.$"} :step/id #uuid "e9dff08f-68e1-5fe8-9586-d7f8edd2598c" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425951}}] :activity/title "Gaussian Elimination For NxM Systems of Equations" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425937}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046659} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492937} :activity/id #uuid "6e7bba4e-e339-5059-bc4b-363cbe14a29f" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048445 :topic/id #uuid "a01c36d3-5643-5685-845e-29c37e89238f" :topic/math-academy-id 1733} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492937 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115830 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "90d6f3fc-4b07-573d-909e-71ad76038bc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113918} {:answer/id #uuid "66d8f448-8728-5a93-9a65-75b7c8a60923" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2+3z \\\\ 2+3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492423} {:answer/id #uuid "8de04b4a-cc0c-503c-b014-8f1ba934eb81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2-3z \\\\ 2+3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492497} {:answer/id #uuid "977e4b58-8b63-5c8e-b09e-907ea3fc4715" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2-3z \\\\ 3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492510} {:answer/id #uuid "b58da9b9-82d8-54d2-94d7-4d4f9a370f16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2-3z \\\\ 2-3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492582}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492497} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c202514-58b0-57fd-9d4a-d9d9f27c390e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113917}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8cd9c6c5-780e-5f01-93cc-d5e9b9533129" :question/math-academy-id "q-42040" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x+3z=-2 \\\\ x+y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now  \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x+3z=-2 \\\\ y-3z=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=-2-3z \\\\ y=2+3z \\\\ z=z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the latter can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2-3z \\\\ 2+3z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "2361ed3b-bfae-5a29-916a-e207bd92ed86" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492989}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492948 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492840 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c122c68-ba85-506a-9b5d-b7e8d41f11b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492400} {:answer/id #uuid "90746f9d-5a52-5223-86f2-eebad7cce602" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492502} {:answer/id #uuid "a00e12c1-efd1-5bb1-8807-973d94c98793" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492536} {:answer/id #uuid "af7e5af6-3e33-5368-823c-3062f7002694" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492568} {:answer/id #uuid "fcccf2b5-4696-5f4a-92c9-3b29f694860e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492701}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492568} :answer-field/id #uuid "83ab4b9b-dc34-5dc7-8a1e-ba7fb0076d92" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492760}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "22d64530-5ce7-515c-aafe-c528e2fc812f" :question/math-academy-id "q-74834" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned} & x-4y=-1 \\\\  & 2x-7y=0 \\\\  & -4x+15y=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The system is consistent independent\n\nII. The system has no solution\n\nIII. The system is consistent dependent" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -7 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 15 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -7 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 15 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 15 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ are solutions to the third equation $0x+0y=0$, we can remove this equation from the system. So, the corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-4y=-1 \\\\ y=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation we have $y=2$ and substituting this into the first equation yields $x=7.$ So,  we conclude that the system is consistent independent. \n\nAs a result, only statement I is true."} :step/id #uuid "49cc5d2d-b51f-5454-b5d2-2fecc8135eb1" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492950}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492950 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400646 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b14622e0-0a8b-52f6-8bf8-44a04ea90e2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437896} {:answer/id #uuid "422e0298-fb2d-5c6d-a4af-8cba072754ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437897}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186437896} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ddef766-7f45-5b44-b48d-737353d4be25" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438977} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "522be474-9268-5719-9b67-fa3c52635318" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437898} {:answer/id #uuid "37b81bb5-685b-583b-8db4-0245d173fc7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437899}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186437899} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0b79b55-bd9c-5274-8736-1fa18bb4e7d7" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438978} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63da7652-c50c-579a-9313-44ed8eac188b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437900} {:answer/id #uuid "715c6b27-3b25-5248-a7ad-aceb0fe78ca6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437901}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186437900} :answer-field/id #uuid "a893b756-f994-5e2f-ab56-a98d5a543109" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438979}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4890e1ff-ed9a-5558-acd1-bcef01439e04" :question/math-academy-id "q-131722" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 3x-3y=6 \\\\  & -2x+y=-3 \\\\  & 4x-4y=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **II.** The system is consistent independent\n- **III.** The system has no solution" :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ are solutions to the third equation $0x+0y=0$, we can remove this equation from the system. So, the corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y=2 \\\\ y=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation we have $y=-1$ and substituting this into the first equation yields $x=1.$ So,  we conclude that the system is consistent independent. \n\nAs a result, only statement II is true."} :step/id #uuid "4f6ca757-aec4-527a-86a3-ce82de0d867c" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492984}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492984 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492874 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a7b0d87-9712-510c-adb7-5bde077204da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492235} {:answer/id #uuid "58ea3fc2-519f-5eea-8c33-6dce5b9c6e3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492389} {:answer/id #uuid "8133480e-57da-5ca9-9bce-a1b99fc82856" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492477} {:answer/id #uuid "a85d27da-01e0-5767-a1e4-b5479a5241b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492558} {:answer/id #uuid "da15d75f-b174-5630-b7ee-c26933c1301a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492646}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492477} :answer-field/id #uuid "df2effb2-e366-52f0-a14b-bc202d0cbc2c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492799}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7409a043-b196-5341-8318-5b111a0c527e" :question/math-academy-id "q-131725" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned} & 2x-y=3 \\\\  & -4x+(k-5)y=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & k-5 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & k-5 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & k-7 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-y=3 \\\\ (k-7)y=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=7,$ then the second equation is $0=5,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=7.$"} :step/id #uuid "a93f2400-74e9-5bc9-a239-9a89e32c8532"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492989 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344961 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b9a3770-af37-58af-91e7-3430fd2463b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343154} {:answer/id #uuid "71cae964-c567-5585-ab23-7241fb114732" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343221} {:answer/id #uuid "a8f3da90-4b17-5b45-af78-2746f79a0b95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343724} {:answer/id #uuid "ad97781e-f202-56a0-803a-f17ee1a49ca9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343764} {:answer/id #uuid "f0d5b11f-4138-5c57-8bc8-f9f3a404cfaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344356}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344356} :answer-field/id #uuid "6517af05-6089-578f-972a-9310f8010c94" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344664}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a0c28bd7-70de-59aa-93c9-933cbaca4593" :question/math-academy-id "q-74646" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned} & x+4y=2 \\\\  & 2x+(k+1)y=3\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k+1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k+1 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & k-7 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x+4y=2 \\\\ (k-7)y=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=7,$ then the second equation is $0=-1,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=7.$"} :step/id #uuid "b7e356b4-fa42-567c-864c-79ee57dd45e6" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492948}}] :activity/title "Gaussian Elimination For NxM Systems of Equations" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492210}]}
